---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Colorist Tool Kit Pro Support">
  <h1>Colorist Tool Kit Pro Support</h1>
  <p>
    Support, troubleshooting, and licensing information for the Colorist Tool Kit Pro
    iOS app and macOS desktop receiver.
  </p>

  <h2>Downloads</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/downloads/ColoristToolKit-Pro-Instructions.pdf" download>
        Download Installation Instructions (PDF)
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The macOS version is available in the <a href="/webshop">webshop</a> and on
    the App Store.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting Started</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Download Colorist Tool Kit Pro from the App Store.</li>
    <li>Launch the app and allow camera access when prompted.</li>
    <li>Tap the probe icon to start a live measurement session.</li>
    <li>Point your iPhone camera at the reference patch or display area you want to measure.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>iPhone running iOS 16 or later</li>
    <li>A supported reference target or display for calibration work</li>
    <li>Same Wi-Fi network as your desktop when streaming measurements</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Measurements do not appear on the desktop:</strong> Make sure both devices
      are on the same Wi-Fi network and that the desktop receiver is running.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Camera preview is dark or frozen:</strong> Force-quit the app and relaunch.
      Ensure camera permissions are enabled in iOS Settings → Colorist Tool Kit Pro → Camera.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Readings seem unstable:</strong> Hold the phone steady and allow a few seconds
      for the measurement to settle. Avoid reflections and uneven lighting on the target.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>App crashes at launch:</strong> Update to the latest iOS version and reinstall
      the app from the App Store.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Licensing &amp; Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    Colorist Tool Kit Pro is available as a one-time purchase through the App Store.
    If you have questions about licensing, upgrades, or volume purchases, please email us.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact Support</h2>
  <p>
    Need more help? Email
    <a href="mailto:stuartblakejones@mac.com">stuartblakejones@mac.com</a>.
  </p>
</Layout>
